---
import { Picture } from 'astro:assets';
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import CallToAction from '../../components/CallToAction.astro';
import PageHero from '../../components/PageHero.astro';
import heroPhoto from '../../assets/communities/park-city/park-city-sign-hero-kansastourism.jpg';
import arenaPhoto from '../../assets/communities/park-city/park-city-hartman-arena-travelks.png';
import casinoPhoto from '../../assets/communities/park-city/park-city-crosswinds-casino-travelks.jpg';
import gilleysPhoto from '../../assets/communities/park-city/park-city-gilleys-self-owned.jpg';
import speedwayPhoto from '../../assets/communities/park-city/park-city-81-speedway-travelks.jpg';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Park City, Kansas Community Guide | Charity Menefee"
  description="A practical introduction to Park City, Kansas, including its location north of Wichita, housing development, event venues, parks, and property considerations."
  pageClass="page-interior page-park-city"
>
  <PageHero
    eyebrow="Community guide · Park City"
    title="Room to live. Places to go."
    intro="Park City is an incorporated community immediately north of Wichita, with residential areas, newer development, and a visible collection of entertainment and event venues."
    image={heroPhoto}
    imageAlt="Colorful Park City sign outside a civic building under a dramatic sky"
    variant="community"
    imagePosition="center center"
    imagePositionMobile="36% center"
  />

  <section class="section-space" aria-labelledby="park-city-overview-title">
    <div class="shell editorial-grid">
      <div data-reveal="left">
        <p class="eyebrow">Getting oriented</p>
        <h2 id="park-city-overview-title">An independent city along the north side of the metro.</h2>
      </div>
      <div class="prose" data-reveal="right">
        <p>Park City is immediately north of Wichita along I-135. It's its own incorporated city, established in 1980, rather than simply a northern part of Wichita.</p>
        <p>Residential neighborhoods make up much of the community, while major venues along the I-135 and Broadway side give Park City an event and entertainment presence that's particularly visible across the Wichita area.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section-space section-surface" aria-labelledby="park-city-housing-title">
    <div class="shell editorial-grid">
      <div data-reveal="left">
        <p class="eyebrow">Homes and subdivisions</p>
        <h2 id="park-city-housing-title">Established areas and newer development create different choices.</h2>
      </div>
      <div class="prose" data-reveal="right">
        <p>Park City's housing includes established residential areas and newer development. The City's New Homes page identifies Cambridge Valley, Park Centre, Ironstone Community, and Prairie Hills 4th among the development examples.</p>
        <p>Those names provide broad context rather than confirming that a particular home or lot is available. Compare the age and construction of the home, the lot, neighborhood pattern, and any obligations tied to the property.</p>
        <p>Location within Park City can also affect how directly a property connects to I-135, Broadway, and other north Wichita routes. The roads you'd actually use are more informative than a generalized description of access.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section-space section-sage" aria-labelledby="park-city-entertainment-title">
    <div class="shell">
      <div class="section-heading split-heading">
        <div data-reveal="left">
          <p class="eyebrow">Entertainment and events</p>
          <h2 id="park-city-entertainment-title">Park City is known for some of the area's bigger entertainment venues.</h2>
        </div>
        <div class="prose" data-reveal="right">
          <p>The area around I-135 and Broadway includes several well-known entertainment destinations, including Heartland Credit Union Arena, CrossWinds Casino, Gilley's, and 81 Speedway.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="park-city-venue-grid reveal-stagger">
        <figure class="park-city-venue-card" data-reveal="left-scale">
          <Picture
            src={arenaPhoto}
            formats={['avif', 'webp']}
            widths={[480, 720, 960, 1200]}
            sizes="(min-width: 48rem) 50vw, 100vw"
            alt="Box office entrance at Heartland Credit Union Arena in Park City"
          />
          <figcaption><strong>Heartland Credit Union Arena</strong><span>A regional event venue and a recognizable Park City destination.</span></figcaption>
        </figure>
        <figure class="park-city-venue-card" data-reveal="right-scale">
          <Picture
            src={casinoPhoto}
            formats={['avif', 'webp']}
            widths={[480, 720, 960, 1200]}
            sizes="(min-width: 48rem) 50vw, 100vw"
            alt="CrossWinds Casino exterior in Park City at dusk"
          />
          <figcaption><strong>CrossWinds Casino</strong><span>Part of the entertainment presence along Park City's major north-side corridors.</span></figcaption>
        </figure>
        <figure class="park-city-venue-card" data-reveal="left-scale">
          <Picture
            src={gilleysPhoto}
            formats={['avif', 'webp']}
            widths={[480, 720, 960, 1200]}
            sizes="(min-width: 48rem) 50vw, 100vw"
            alt="Illuminated Gilley's sign at dusk in Park City, with cars filling the parking lot"
          />
          <figcaption><strong>Gilley's</strong><span>A visible entertainment venue near Park City's other destination uses.</span></figcaption>
        </figure>
        <figure class="park-city-venue-card park-city-venue-speedway" data-reveal="right-scale">
          <Picture
            src={speedwayPhoto}
            formats={['avif', 'webp']}
            widths={[480, 720, 960, 1200]}
            sizes="(min-width: 48rem) 50vw, 100vw"
            alt="Race cars and spectators at 81 Speedway in Park City"
          />
          <figcaption><strong>81 Speedway</strong><span>A motorsports venue that adds another distinct event setting to the city.</span></figcaption>
        </figure>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section-space" aria-labelledby="park-city-parks-title">
    <div class="shell editorial-grid">
      <div data-reveal="left">
        <p class="eyebrow">Parks and everyday recreation</p>
        <h2 id="park-city-parks-title">Municipal parks provide a quieter part of daily life.</h2>
      </div>
      <div class="prose" data-reveal="right">
        <p>Park City's municipal park system provides a quieter counterpoint to its larger venues. Osage Trail Park includes a pond, picnic shelter, and walking path, while Prairie Wind Park includes playgrounds and a walking path that extends through Poston Park and Habiger Park.</p>
        <p>Other municipal spaces include Hap McLean Park, Jardine Memorial Park, Primrose Park, and Senior Center Park. Together, the park system adds everyday walking, recreation, and gathering spaces beyond the city's larger destination venues.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section-space section-surface" aria-labelledby="park-city-practical-title">
    <div class="shell editorial-grid">
      <div data-reveal="left">
        <p class="eyebrow">Practical things to consider</p>
        <h2 id="park-city-practical-title">The specific location can shape how the property functions.</h2>
      </div>
      <div class="prose" data-reveal="right">
        <p>Start by deciding whether you want to compare an established residential area, a newer subdivision, or both. Then consider whether the address is closer to the entertainment and event corridors or farther inside a residential area.</p>
        <p>Review its connections to I-135, Broadway, and the roads you expect to use. The home's age, lot characteristics, development pattern, and any property-specific obligations provide the next level of comparison.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section-space" aria-labelledby="park-city-search-title">
    <div class="shell">
      <div class="section-heading split-heading">
        <div data-reveal="left">
          <p class="eyebrow">Useful questions</p>
          <h2 id="park-city-search-title">What should you compare when looking in Park City?</h2>
        </div>
        <p data-reveal="right">The most useful answers come from the individual property, its development, and the routes around it.</p>
      </div>
      <ul class="question-grid reveal-stagger">
        <li data-reveal="up">Would you rather compare an established neighborhood, newer development, or both?</li>
        <li data-reveal="up">How does this location connect to I-135, Broadway, and the destinations you use most?</li>
        <li data-reveal="up">Would you prefer to be closer to Park City's entertainment and event side or farther from it?</li>
        <li data-reveal="up">Which HOA requirements, restrictions, lot characteristics, or included improvements are tied to this property?</li>
        <li data-reveal="up">How does this part of Park City compare with the nearby areas you're also considering?</li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </section>

  <nav class="shell next-community" aria-label="Community pages">
    <span>Keep exploring</span>
    <a href="/communities/">All communities <i aria-hidden="true">→</i></a>
  </nav>
  <CallToAction
    title="Have questions about a property in Park City?"
    copy="If you're comparing communities or have questions about a specific property, tell me what you're considering. I’ll help you sort through the location and property details that matter."
  />
</BaseLayout>
